# Filament conventions

## Resources

- One `Resource` per model under `app/Filament/Resources/`
- Pages in `{Resource}/Pages/` (List, Create, Edit, View as needed)
- Relation managers in `{Resource}/RelationManagers/`
- Delegate business logic to `App\Services\api\v1\*` — resources wire UI only

## Table actions → dedicated classes

Do **not** inline complex `Action::make()` logic in resources. Use classes under `app/Filament/Actions/`:

| Kind | Path examples |
|------|----------------|
| Table status actions | `Actions/Status/ApproveAction`, `RejectAction`, `ResetAction` |
| Question-specific | `Actions/Question/ApproveQuestionAction`, `RejectQuestionAction` |
| Form/modal actions | `Actions/Forms/Status/...` |
| Bulk delete | `Actions/Delete/DeleteBulkAction`, `ForceDeleteBulkAction` |

Table actions extend `Filament\Tables\Actions\Action`, call services in `->action()`, check policies with `auth()->user()->can()`.

## Reusable columns & filters

Extract repeated table UI into shared classes:

- **Status column**: `App\Filament\Columns\Status\StatusColumn::make()` — badge + `Status::colorByValue()` (workflow `StatusInterface`, not soft deletes)
- **Trashed column**: `App\Filament\Columns\Trash\TrashedColumn::make()` — Active/Trashed badge from `deleted_at` / `trashed()`
- **User column**: `App\Filament\Columns\User\UserColumn::make()` — username, user icon, full name in description, search via `User::matchingSearchTerm()`
- **Status filter**: `App\Filament\Filters\Status\StatusFilter::make()` — options from `Status::options()`
- **User filter**: `App\Filament\Filters\User\UserFilter::make()` — relationship `user` / `username`, includes banned and soft-deleted users in options
- **Date between filter**: `App\Filament\Filters\Date\BetweenFilter::make()` — `from` / `until` date pickers, `whereDate` on a column (default `created_at`)
- **Forms**: `App\Filament\Forms/Status/StatusSelect`, notification helpers in `Forms/Notification/`

Register in resource `table()`:

```php
->columns([StatusColumn::make(), TrashedColumn::make(), UserColumn::make(), /* … */])
->filters([StatusFilter::make(), TrashedFilter::make(), UserFilter::make(), BetweenFilter::make()])
```

## User relation column (mandatory)

For Filament **table** or **relation manager** columns that display a related **User** (`user.username` or `{relation}.username`):

- **MUST** use `App\Filament\Columns\User\UserColumn::make()` (default column: `user.username`, relationship: `user`).
- **MUST NOT** inline `TextColumn::make('user.username')` with duplicate icon, description, or `whereHas` + `matchingSearchTerm` search logic.
- For another relationship name, pass the column path — relationship is taken from the segment before `.`: `UserColumn::make('author.username')`.
- Extra presentation (e.g. `->wrap()`) may be chained on the returned column.

```php
use App\Filament\Columns\User\UserColumn;

->columns([
    UserColumn::make(),
])
```

Reference: `CommentResource`, `UserNotificationResource`.

## User relation filter (mandatory)

For Filament **table** or **relation manager** filters by related **User** (`user` or `user_id` on the parent model):

- **MUST** use `App\Filament\Filters\User\UserFilter::make()` (default filter name: `user`, relationship: `user`).
- **MUST NOT** inline `SelectFilter::make('user_id')` / `SelectFilter::make('user')` with duplicate `relationship('user', 'username')`, `NotBannedScope`, and `withTrashed()` logic.
- Use `UserFilter::make('user_id')` when the filter attribute is the foreign key column name.
- Extra options (e.g. `->preload()`) may be chained on the returned filter.

```php
use App\Filament\Filters\User\UserFilter;

->filters([
    UserFilter::make(),
    // or UserFilter::make('user_id'),
])
```

Reference: `CommentResource`, `UserNotificationResource`.

## Date range filter (mandatory)

For Filament **table** or **relation manager** filters that constrain a **date/datetime column** by an inclusive **from / until** range:

- **MUST** use `App\Filament\Filters\Date\BetweenFilter::make()` (default filter name and column: `created_at`).
- **MUST NOT** inline `Filter::make('created_at')` with duplicate `DatePicker` `from`/`until` fields and `whereDate` query logic.
- Use `BetweenFilter::make('updated_at')` for other columns; optional third argument for a custom label, or chain `->label()` on the returned filter.
- Pass a second argument when the filter name differs from the queried column: `BetweenFilter::make('period', 'created_at')`.

```php
use App\Filament\Filters\Date\BetweenFilter;

->filters([
    BetweenFilter::make(),
])
```

Reference: `CommentResource`.

## Soft deletes (mandatory)

For any Filament **table** or **relation manager** on a model that uses Laravel `SoftDeletes` (`deleted_at`):

- **MUST** add `App\Filament\Filters\Trash\TrashedFilter::make()` to `->filters([...])`.
- **MUST** add `App\Filament\Columns\Trash\TrashedColumn::make()` when the table shows an Active/Trashed status badge column.
- **MUST** use `->withTrashed()` in the resource/relation manager `getEloquentQuery()` or `modifyQueryUsing` when the list should show trashed rows (same pattern as `QuestionResource`).
- **MUST NOT** implement a custom `TernaryFilter` (or inline `deleted_at` filter) for trash/active/all — even if planning docs suggest custom labels. Reuse `TrashedFilter`; extend that class in `app/Filament/Filters/Trash/` only if labels or query logic must change project-wide.
- **MUST NOT** inline `TextColumn::make('deleted_at')` with badge, `getStateUsing`, and color for Active/Trashed — use `TrashedColumn::make()`.

```php
use App\Filament\Columns\Trash\TrashedColumn;
use App\Filament\Filters\Trash\TrashedFilter;

// in table():
->columns([
    TrashedColumn::make(),
])
->filters([
    TrashedFilter::make(),
    // other filters…
])
```

Reference: `QuestionResource`, `TagResource`, `CompanyResource`, `CommentResource`.

## Status workflow

Models implementing `App\Interfaces\v1\Status\StatusInterface` use shared status actions (`ApproveAction`, etc.) and `StatusService` for transitions. Hide actions when `!$record->can('changeStatus')` or terminal state (e.g. `isApproved()`).

## Widgets & infolists

- Widgets: `app/Filament/Resources/Widgets/` or `Resources/{Resource}/Widgets/`
- Custom pages: `app/Filament/Pages/` (e.g. settings, mass notifications)

## Traits

Shared form/table behavior: `app/Traits/Filament/` (e.g. `WithRelatedSelects`).
